        "title": "Not convinced",
        "text": "I felt it was a bit of a shame to turn the process of death into a tourist attraction.  If you have a genuine interest in Hinduism and cremation from a spiritual perspective I would definitely say go.  We were there on a day when there was a politicians cremation and learning about the process was interesting, but I still felt it was a bit voyeuristic. The sadhus who wander around seem to be a part of the money making process and I wasn't convinced of their spiritual integrity.  This is the only place in Kathmandu where we were really hassled by street hawkers.",
