      {
        "review_id": 215314207,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r215314207-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Commercialized Exploitation",
        "text": "Pashupatinath temple is tauted as one of the most significant Hindu temples of Shiva in the world. The temple is located on the banks of the Bagmati River in the eastern part of Kathmandu and serves as not only a place of worship for Hindus, but also a crematory. \n\nPlain and simply, Pashupatinath Temple is a tourist trap. \n\nEntrance for non-Asians is $10 (1,000 nrs) and that's the first opportunity to fork over money... \nBombarded with people offering a \"guided\" tour, the average tourist will get fleeced out of money by those looking to earn a quick buck. The Sadhus (Hindu holy men) were opportunistic as well, charging people for photo ops.  \n\nThe temple complex has a very dark and ominous feel... and something about all of the tourists taking pictures of the funeral pyres and grieving families just doesn't seem fitting or respectful.\n\nSave the 1000 rupees for momo's or a walk around Bhaktapur!",
        "review_tip": null,
