        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r213844534-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "beware",
        "text": "Pashupatinath temple in Kathmandu may be considered as one of the holiest Hindu shrines. But beware while visiting the area. There is a gang of robbers operating around and in the temple which the local police have been unable to bust. They steal and rob travellers of their valuables by diverting their attention in talks related to the temple under the pretext of helping them. Many have lost their money, expensive mobiles and the like. Also a person claiming to be the priest will ask you for money (nrs 1000 plus negotiable) to take you inside the temple by another route bypassing the crowd. This implies that if you have money you are allowed to see the shrine faster unlike others who may have to wait because they do not have money enough to pay the priest. And this all when they claim that God treats all humans equal. The area is also very crowded and not so clean.",
